__label__books english literature about the author william joseph long 1866 1952 was an american writer naturalist and minister he lived and worked in stamford connecticut as a minister of the first congregationalist church as a naturalist he would leave stamford every march often with his son brian and two daughters lois and cesca to travel to the wilderness of maine there they would stay until the first snows of october although sometimes he would stay all winter in the 1920s he began spending his summers in nova scotia claiming the wilderness is getting too crowded
